s that are lethal or highly deleterious in the homozygous state can persist in a population because the allele is not expressed (and therefore does not select against the carrier) in the heterozygous state.\n    *   Heterozygous individuals (carriers) do not show symptoms and can reproduce.\n\n    *   The explanation fits (G) \"Heterozygous individuals will show\n"}
