 Message Authenticity: Relates to source, not necessarily the \"exactness\" of the content (though integrity is part of it).\n    *   (F) Message Reliability: Often used in networking (TCP), but \"Integrity\" is the standard computer science/security term for \"exactly as they were sent\".\n\n    *   The question asks for the term describing data arriving exactly as sent.\n    *\n"}
