tion (C) provides a comprehensive definition based on recognized international standards (like those of the FAO).\n\n    *   \"Let's think step by step. Food security is a state where all people have physical, social, and economic access to sufficient, safe, and nutritious food. According to the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO), food security is achieved when four key pillars are met\n"}
