+{"question_index": 19, "question_id": 9448, "category": "physics", "k": 1, "gold": "F", "parsed_letter": "C", "correct": false, "full_text": "*   Arm length ($r$) = 70.0 cm = 0.70 m.\n    *   Angle of swing ($\\Delta\\theta$) = 45\u00b0 = 45\u00b0 $\\times$ ($\\pi / 180$\u00b0) = $\\pi / 4$ radians.\n    *   Time of swing ($\\Delta t$) = 0.5 s.\n    *   Assume constant speed during the swing (this is a simplification, but let's work with it).\n    *   Blood drop mass ($m$) = 1.0 g = 0.001 kg.\n    *   Goal: Find the acceleration ($a$) of the blood drop at the bottom of the swing.\n\n    *   The arm is swinging like a pendulum.\n    *   The tip of the arm (where the blood drop is) moves in a circular arc.\n    *   The velocity ($v$) of the tip is $v = \\omega r$, where $\\omega$ is the angular velocity.\n    *   The angular velocity $\\omega$ can be approximated as $\\Delta\\theta / \\Delta t$.\n    *   $\\omega = (\\pi / 4) / 0.5 = \\pi / 2$ rad/s.\n    *   The speed $v$ at the tip is $v = (\\pi / 2) \\times 0.70$ m/s.\n    *   $v = 0.35\\pi$ m/s $\\approx 1.0995$ m/s.\n\n    *   At the bottom of the swing, the acceleration of the blood drop has two components:\n        1.  Tangential acceleration ($a_t$): Since we assume constant speed, $a_t = 0$.\n        2.  Centripetal acceleration ($a_c$): $a_c = v^2 / r$.\n\n    *   $a_c = v^2 / r$\n    *   $v = 0.35\\pi$\n    *   $a_c = (0.35\\pi)^2 / 0.70$\n    *   $a_c = (0.1225 \\pi^2) / 0.70$\n    *\n"}
