+{"question_index": 19, "question_id": 9448, "category": "physics", "k": 3, "gold": "F", "parsed_letter": "C", "correct": false, "full_text": "*   Arm length ($L$) = 70.0 cm = 0.70 m.\n    *   Angle of swing ($\\Delta\\theta$) = 45\u00b0 = $\\pi/4$ radians.\n    *   Time for swing ($\\Delta t$) = 0.5 s.\n    *   Assumption: Constant speed ($v$) during the swing.\n    *   Mass of a blood drop ($m$) = 1.0 g = 0.001 kg (though mass isn't needed for acceleration).\n    *   Question: What is the acceleration ($a$) at the bottom of the swing?\n\n    *   The arm moves through $\\Delta\\theta = \\pi/4$ radians in $\\Delta t = 0.5$ s.\n    *   Angular velocity ($\\omega$) = $\\Delta\\theta / \\Delta t = (\\pi/4) / 0.5 = \\pi/2$ rad/s.\n    *   The tangential speed ($v$) is $v = \\omega \\cdot L = (\\pi/2) \\cdot 0.70$ m/s.\n\n    *   At the bottom of the swing, the arm's path is circular (assuming the shoulder joint is the center).\n    *   The acceleration at the bottom of a circular path is the centripetal acceleration ($a_c$).\n    *   $a_c = v^2 / L$ or $a_c = \\omega^2 \\cdot L$.\n\n    *   $\\omega = \\pi/2$ rad/s.\n    *   $a_c = (\\pi/2)^2 \\cdot 0.70$.\n    *   $\\pi \\approx 3.14159$.\n    *   $\\pi/2 \\approx 1.5708$.\n    *   $(\\pi/2)^2 \\approx 2.4674$.\n    *   $a_c = 2.4674 \\cdot 0.70$.\n    *   $a_c \\approx 1.727$ m/s\u00b2.\n\n    *   (A) 1.22\n    *   (B) 2.45\n    *   (C) 1.9\n"}
+{"question_index": 19, "question_id": 9448, "category": "physics", "k": 4, "gold": "F", "parsed_letter": "B", "correct": false, "full_text": "*   Arm length ($L$) = 70.0 cm = 0.7 m.\n    *   Angular swing ($\\Delta \\theta$) = 45\u00b0 = $\\pi/4$ radians.\n    *   Time for one swing ($\\Delta t$) = 0.5 s.\n    *   Assume constant angular speed ($\\omega$).\n    *   $\\omega = \\Delta \\theta / \\Delta t = (\\pi/4) / 0.5 = \\pi/2$ rad/s.\n    *   Mass of blood drop ($m$) = 1.0 g = 0.001 kg.\n    *   The blood drop is at the *bottom* of the swing.\n    *   Question: What is the *acceleration* ($a$) of the blood drop at the bottom of the swing?\n\n    *   The blood drop is moving in a circular arc.\n    *   At the bottom of the swing, the acceleration has two components:\n        1.  Tangential acceleration ($a_t$): Since the angular speed $\\omega$ is assumed constant, the tangential acceleration $a_t = 0$.\n        2.  Centripetal (radial) acceleration ($a_c$): $a_c = \\omega^2 r$, where $r$ is the radius of the arc (arm length $L$).\n\n    *   $a_c = \\omega^2 L$\n    *   $\\omega = \\pi/2$ rad/s\n    *   $L = 0.7$ m\n    *   $a_c = (\\pi/2)^2 \\times 0.7$\n    *   $a_c = (\\pi^2 / 4) \\times 0.7$\n    *   $\\pi^2 \\approx 9.8696$\n    *   $a_c = (9.8696 / 4) \\times 0.7$\n    *   $a_c = 2.4674 \\times 0.7$\n    *   $a_c = 1.72718$ m/s\u00b2\n\n    *   (A) 1.22\n    *   (B) 2.45\n    \n"}
